type":"CHP","year":"2025"},"chapteredDate":"2025-10-01","committees":[],"conditions":[{"ruleId":"ca-cond-1","text":"Section 2.5 of this bill incorporates amendments to Section 15104 of the Elections Code proposed by both this bill and Senate Bill 3. That section of this bill shall become operative only if (1) both bills are enacted and become effective on or before January 1, 2026, (2) each bill amends Section 15104 of the Elections Code, and (3) this bill is enacted after Senate Bill 3, in which case Section 2 of this bill shall not become operative.","versionId":"20250AB1695CHP"}],"contentHash":"cad15811f814be6955f510db57b547b6086c59741793142c3ce54c787eecbc7b","cosponsorCount":null,"digest":"Existing law requires elections officials to begin mailing ballots to every registered voter no later than 29 days before an election. Existing law authorizes a jurisdiction to begin processing vote by mail ballot return envelopes and, if the jurisdiction has the necessary computer capability, vote by mail ballots 29 days before an election.\n\nThis bill would authorize elections officials to begin processing vote by mail ballot return envelopes and vote by mail ballots on the date on which the ballots are mailed, thereby allowing elections officials to begin processing vote by mail return envelopes and ballots earlier than 29 days before an election.\n\nThis bill would incorporate additional changes to Section 15104 of the Elections Code proposed by SB 3 to be operative only if this bill and SB 3 are enacted and this bill is enacted last.","digestDate":null,"digestVersion":null,"effective":{"basis":"not_verified","date":null,"note":"No effective date is recorded in the official bill data and DemocracyHQ has not verified one. A non-urgency statute enacted in a regular session generally takes effect on January 1 after a 90-day period (Cal. Const. art. IV, § 8(c)), but a bill may state other operative dates. The text also makes all or part of the measure conditional; the conditions are quoted on this page, and whether they were met is not recorded here."},"expiryClauses":[],"firstObservedAt":"2026-11-20T01:12:59Z","id":"ca-20252026-ab16","identifier":"AB 16","indicators":{"Appropriation":"NO","BudgetBill":"NO","Election":"NO","FiscalCommittee":"NO","ImmediateEffect":"NO","LocalProgram":"NO","TaxLevy":"NO","Urgency":"NO","UsualCurrentExpenses":"NO","VoteRequired":"MAJORITY"},"introducedDate":"2024-12-02","issueTags":[{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"official subject line","matchedText":"Vote by mail ballots: processing.","ruleId":"tag-mail-2","tag":"mail-voting"},{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"official subject line","matchedText":"Vote by mail ballots: processing.","ruleId":"tag-admin-2","tag":"election-administration"}],"judicialNote":"Legislative status does not show whether a court has blocked, narrowed or upheld any provision. Check the linked litigation, which may be incomplete.","lastActionDate":"2025-10-01","lastActionText":"Chaptered by Secretary of State - Chapter 140, Statutes of 2025.","lastCheckedAt":"2026-11-22T17:54:55Z","leadAuthors":"Introduced by Assembly Member Alanis","legislativeStatus":{"currentHouse":"Secretary of State","currentLocation":null,"currentStatus":"Chaptered","measureState":"Chaptered"},"legislativeSubjects":[],"measureType":"Assembly Bill","officialUrl":"https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billNavClient.xhtml?bill_id=202520260AB16","policyArea":null,"relatedMeasures":[],"selection":{"matchedField":"official subject line (latest version)","matchedText":"Vote by mail","ruleId":"ca-select-2"},"session":"2025-2026 Regular Session","shortTitles":[],"sourceId":"ca-leginfo-bulk","sourcePublishedAt":"2026-11-16T05:26:36Z","sourceRecordUrl":null,"sponsors":[],"state":"06","stateAbbr":"CA","subject":"Vote by mail ballots: processing.","title":"An act to amend Sections 15101 and 15104 of the Elections Code, relating to elections.","verification":{"checkedAt":"2026-11-22T17:54:55Z","method":"automated_prima